[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c7bf2d22-67db-5bfb-9d76-d999020db50d" "question-6e1139bd-70c8-5172-a11e-474495b10da9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c7bf2d22-67db-5bfb-9d76-d999020db50d" :question/id #uuid "c7bf2d22-67db-5bfb-9d76-d999020db50d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105190" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $[0,15]$\n\nII. $(-3,5]\\cup [6,8)$\n\nIII. $(1,6)$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(1,6)$ is open. The boundary points are $1$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not open because:\n\n- $[0,15]$ has two boundary points $0$, and $15$, and both of them lie in the set.\n\n- $(-3,5]\\cup [6,8)$ has four boundary points $-3$, $5$, $6$, and $8$, and the points $5$ and $6$ lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c9d3d2d-5c89-5028-8119-349ee1ac7225"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c9d3d2d-5c89-5028-8119-349ee1ac7225" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c9d3d2d-5c89-5028-8119-349ee1ac7225" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-df327c23-f0d8-51b7-8f66-04274266589e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5ff4f3ba-42e5-570f-bca8-ed45b21cb1f7" "answer-1ed67d77-19b4-542e-9fbf-7d6adca9ad93" "answer-c0c57c73-2803-51dc-b2db-124289558110" "answer-e09f8edf-88de-5e68-86d0-9a2c8f07968e" "answer-df327c23-f0d8-51b7-8f66-04274266589e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ff4f3ba-42e5-570f-bca8-ed45b21cb1f7" :answer/id #uuid "5ff4f3ba-42e5-570f-bca8-ed45b21cb1f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ed67d77-19b4-542e-9fbf-7d6adca9ad93" :answer/id #uuid "1ed67d77-19b4-542e-9fbf-7d6adca9ad93" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c0c57c73-2803-51dc-b2db-124289558110" :answer/id #uuid "c0c57c73-2803-51dc-b2db-124289558110" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e09f8edf-88de-5e68-86d0-9a2c8f07968e" :answer/id #uuid "e09f8edf-88de-5e68-86d0-9a2c8f07968e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-df327c23-f0d8-51b7-8f66-04274266589e" :answer/id #uuid "df327c23-f0d8-51b7-8f66-04274266589e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186193325 :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nI. $[1,2]\\cup [3,4]$\n\nII. $[0,1)$\n\nIII. $[0,1)\\cup (1,2]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $[1,2]\\cup [3,4]$ is closed. It consists of two parts, where the boundary points are $1,2,3,$ and $4.$ All of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other sets are not closed because:\n\n- $[0,1)$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\n- $[0,1)\\cup (1,2]$ has a boundary point $1$, which does not lie in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186191877 :answer-field/correct 17592186191878 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6e1139bd-70c8-5172-a11e-474495b10da9" :question/id #uuid "6e1139bd-70c8-5172-a11e-474495b10da9" :question/math-academy-id "q-71799" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nI. $(-4,1)$\n\nII. $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$\n\nIII. $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nAmong the given sets, only $(-4,1)$ and $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are open because:\n\n- The boundary points of the set $(-4,1)$ are $-4$, and $1.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\n- The boundary points of the set  $(2,4)\\cup (5,6)$ are $2$, $4$, $5$, and $6.$ None of them lie in the set.\n\nThe other set is not open because $(0,1)\\cup (7,9]$ has four boundary points $0$, $1$, $7$, and $9$, and the point $9$ lies in the set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-088f8fb8-c517-5efa-a60f-bfc3f63f3d91"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-088f8fb8-c517-5efa-a60f-bfc3f63f3d91" :answer-field/id #uuid "088f8fb8-c517-5efa-a60f-bfc3f63f3d91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1ed8fb2e-025d-558e-b734-33e4b83dc4e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1ed8fb2e-025d-558e-b734-33e4b83dc4e1" "answer-f302f02f-61a4-575b-9708-5be939245e79" "answer-ab767696-bebf-5e3e-898c-7b6fb784dec2" "answer-fffeb0c3-dc23-57b1-9396-d4b717c58bd3" "answer-0fe60442-b181-5edf-a66e-97f8860604d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1ed8fb2e-025d-558e-b734-33e4b83dc4e1" :answer/id #uuid "1ed8fb2e-025d-558e-b734-33e4b83dc4e1